---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How big a forwarding table is, how finely it can split traffic, how many connections a change can break, and how much extra work the second hop and the wrapping add. A teaching model with round numbers, not Cloudflare's data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Servers in the data center <input type="range" min="10" max="500" step="10" value="300" data-s /> <b data-sval></b></label>
      <label>Buckets per server, at least <input type="range" min="50" max="400" step="10" value="100" data-m /> <b data-mval></b></label>
      <label>A server is this much above the average load (%) <input type="range" min="5" max="50" step="5" value="20" data-x /> <b data-xval></b></label>
      <label>Size of a packet before wrapping (bytes) <input type="range" min="576" max="1500" step="12" value="1500" data-p /> <b data-pval></b></label>
      <label>Packets per second the data center forwards (millions) <input type="range" min="1" max="100" value="10" data-q /> <b data-qval></b></label>
      <label>Share of packets taking the second hop (%) <input type="range" min="0" max="5" step="0.5" value="1" data-h /> <b data-hval></b></label>
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, not Cloudflare's system or data. From Cloudflare's 2020 post: the table is a power of 2 in size, it has more than 100 times as many buckets as servers, the second hop is usually taken by fewer than 1% of forwarded packets, and a 1500-byte packet becomes 1536 bytes once wrapped (a 36 byte increase). My own assumptions, which you can change: 300 servers, 10 million packets per second, and that each slot of a bucket holds a 4-byte IPv4 address. "Hash mod N" is a plain stand-in for a scheme that rehashes when the server count changes, as Cloudflare says ECMP does; the post does not give ECMP's exact formula. Other assumptions: connections spread evenly over buckets, a server's load is proportional to its buckets, and a server is drained with a single change to each of its buckets.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 12; // lines in the result list
    const WRAP_BYTES = 36; // 1536 - 1500: what wrapping adds to a packet, from Cloudflare's post
    const LINK_BYTES = 1500; // the usual largest packet on the Internet
    const SLOT_BYTES = 4, SLOTS = 2, KB = 1024, MILLION = 1e6;
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => (n >= 100 ? Math.round(n) : Math.round(n * 10) / 10).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const pct = (n: number) => `${fmt(n)}%`;
    // smallest power of 2 that is strictly more than the target
    const pow2Above = (n: number) => { let p = 1; while (p <= n) p *= 2; return p; };
    function draw() {
      ['s', 'm', 'x', 'p', 'q', 'h'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const servers = val('[data-s]'); const mult = val('[data-m]'); const over = val('[data-x]');
      const inner = val('[data-p]'); const pps = val('[data-q]') * MILLION; const hop = val('[data-h]');
      const table = pow2Above(servers * mult);
      const perServer = table / servers;
      const outer = inner + WRAP_BYTES;
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Buckets in the table (a power of 2)', fmt(table)],
        ['Buckets per server, on average', fmt(perServer)],
        ['Share of connections one bucket stands for', `1 in ${fmt(table)}`],
        ['Table size with two 4-byte slots per bucket (KB)', fmt((table * SLOT_BYTES * SLOTS) / KB)],
        ['Connections that change server when one leaves, hash mod N', pct((100 * (servers - 1)) / servers)],
        ['Connections that lose their server when one is drained, one slot per bucket', pct(100 / servers)],
        ['Connections that lose their server when one is drained, two slots per bucket', '0%'],
        [`Buckets to move off a server ${over}% above the average`, fmt((perServer * over) / (100 + over))],
        ['Share of connections that move to other servers when those buckets move', pct((100 * perServer * over) / (100 + over) / table)],
        ['Packet size after wrapping (bytes)', fmt(outer)],
        ['Does the wrapped packet fit in a 1500-byte link?', outer <= LINK_BYTES ? 'yes' : 'no, needs jumbo frames'],
        ['Packets per second that take the second hop', fmt((pps * hop) / 100)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
